  "id": "neuromarketing",
  "term": "neuromarketing",
  "definition": "Neuromarketing is the use of neuroscience-based methods to study what drives consumers’ choices and responses. It examines reactions to advertisements or products, such as through measures like eye movements, to inform advertising and brand promotion.",
